# The stored value may be more than a number (a sum with a generic arm; a cast). The list is written as number[]: its storage is of integers or of doubles far more often than of any value, so no storage is guessed.
# In a loop the code then has an arm for each kind that may hold the value (of any value, of doubles, of integers, in that order), and each arm tests that the value fits. Outside loops the arm for any value stands alone, as it did under the guess.
# RUN(SUM): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# SUM: = PutArrayElement
# SUM-NOT: arrayStorage=Contiguous
# RUN(CAST): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# CAST: = PutArrayElement
# CAST-NOT: arrayStorage=Contiguous
# Fifteen values (numbers, a text, null, undefined, a bigint, a list, an object, a symbol) into six kinds of list at five positions, three turns each.
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
